// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Author: Simone Machetti
//
// Description:
//   Self-checking testbench for the full SQUARE PE datapath. It is the
//   equivalence oracle for the square variant: the whole path
//     disp_array_a_sqr / disp_array_b_sqr
//        -> pe_array_sqr | pe_array_alpha_sqr | pe_array_beta_sqr  (parallel)
//        -> const_sqr -> acc_array_sqr
//   must produce, at pe_out, the SAME plain matrix multiply as the baseline
//   disp_array -> pe_array -> acc_array. So the golden, packing and result
//   reconstruction are reused verbatim from tb_acc_array; only the DUT and the
//   per-mode controls (square dispatch centering, idle-zero, complex negate,
//   const select) change. For each of the 11 modes:
//
//     1. Define the A, B and X matrices for the mode (shapes from modes.xlsx).
//     2. Fill A and B with corner-biased random signed values.
//     3. Compute the golden X = A * B (real, or complex with 4 real products).
//     4. Pack A and B into the two 256-bit operand words at the Storage-table
//        positions (SEL only drives routing in the DUT, never placement).
//     5. Run the square path and read pe_out; reconstruct each result from its
//        lane (L0) or fused {H(even), L(odd)} 40-bit pair (L1..L3). The square
//        accumulator applies the exact /2, so pe_out is the true result.
//     6. Compare each golden X element against the pe_out that carries it.
//
//   Two passes: single-shot (acc_i = 0) checks the resolved matmul; the
//   accumulation pass loads an external seed (native units - the acc-mux <<1
//   handles the 2x internally) then accumulates the same result NUM_ACC-1 times
//   via feedback and checks pe_out == seed + NUM_ACC * result.
//
// Parameters:
//   NUM_RAND - number of random A,B matrix pairs per mode
//   NUM_ACC  - iterations in the accumulation pass
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

`timescale 1 ns/1 ps

`ifndef CLK_PERIOD_NS
`define CLK_PERIOD_NS 10
`endif

